pr_comments:
@Hoishin as it says you should never have both so if it detects `yarn.lock` and `package-lock` parcel shouldn't even consider this use-case to be any different, meaning use yarn if there is a `yarn.lock`. (this is a personal opinion)

About yarn supporting `package-lock.json` it's not the kinda support you might have hoped for and might be totally irrelevant for this (https://yarnpkg.com/blog/2018/06/04/yarn-import-package-lock/)

A bit more on this if there is a `package-lock` and a `yarn.lock` then either the user is messing up between both which is unlikely (unless they have no clue what they're doing) or the `package-lock` is from `the original repo`/`some other contributor/dev` and in that case using npm wouldn't make any sense as the user currently running parcel prefers yarn. (Just trying to figure out the use-cases where there is a `package-lock` and `yarn.lock` file)

